@startuml
title D&D Simple - Room Realtime Synchronization
autonumber

actor "User A" as UserA
participant "Web Client A\n(Tactical Board)" as ClientA
participant "Web Client A\n(Character Dashboard)" as DashboardA
participant "Express API" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Socket.IO Server" as Socket
participant "Web Client B\n(Tactical Board)" as ClientB

note over ClientB
Already connected to the same room.
end note

UserA -> ClientA : Open or join room board
ClientA -> API : REST load/join room
API -> DB : Load Room, RoomPlayer, boardState via Prisma
DB --> API : Room state
API --> ClientA : Room state and board snapshot

ClientA -> Socket : Connect with bearer token
Socket -> DB : Verify user via Prisma
DB --> Socket : User record
Socket --> ClientA : Socket connected

ClientA -> Socket : room:join(roomCode, characterId)
Socket -> DB : Join room and ensure character token
DB --> Socket : Updated room state
Socket --> ClientA : room:update and acknowledgement
Socket --> ClientB : room:update

UserA -> ClientA : Change tactical board
ClientA -> Socket : board:state(boardState)
Socket -> DB : Persist/process boardState JSON
DB --> Socket : Updated room
Socket --> ClientA : board:update(boardState)
Socket --> ClientB : board:update(boardState)
Socket --> ClientA : Acknowledge update callback

== Room dice-roll history ==

ClientA -> API : GET /rooms/:roomCode/dice-rolls
API -> DB : Load latest 10 public DiceRoll rows by roomId
DB --> API : Shared room dice feed
API --> ClientA : rolls

UserA -> DashboardA : Roll dice in room context
DashboardA -> API : POST /characters/:id/dice-rolls (visibility public, roomCode)
API -> DB : Verify RoomPlayer and persist DiceRoll.roomId
DB --> API : Saved DiceRoll
API --> DashboardA : Saved DiceRoll with id

DashboardA -> Socket : dice:roll(diceRollId)
Socket -> DB : Validate joined room/user/character and DiceRoll.roomId
DB --> Socket : Persisted public roll
Socket --> ClientA : dice:rolled(roll)
Socket --> ClientB : dice:rolled(roll)
ClientA -> ClientA : Merge by id and keep latest 10
ClientB -> ClientB : Merge by id and keep latest 10
@enduml
